1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,227
In this lesson, you'll see how phone
calls work inside Kyntlo: making calls,

2
00:00:05,227 --> 00:00:10,328
listening to recordings and voicemails,
and the feature that wins back lost leads,

3
00:00:10,328 --> 00:00:11,696
missed-call text-back.

4
00:00:12,551 --> 00:00:15,501
Calls live in the same
thread as your messages.

5
00:00:15,501 --> 00:00:20,334
Here's Liam: a Facebook message, then
a phone call, then a confirmation text.

6
00:00:20,334 --> 00:00:25,355
Every call is logged automatically, with
who handled it, and how long it lasted.

7
00:00:26,207 --> 00:00:28,872
Call recording is
included on the Pro plan.

8
00:00:28,872 --> 00:00:30,484
Press play to listen back.

9
00:00:30,484 --> 00:00:35,132
It's great for training new staff, or
for checking exactly what was agreed.

10
00:00:35,132 --> 00:00:38,045
Do let callers know that
calls may be recorded.

11
00:00:38,899 --> 00:00:42,716
To call someone, click the phone
icon at the top of the thread.

12
00:00:42,716 --> 00:00:47,200
Kyntlo calls from your business number,
so the patient sees your practice,

13
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,715
not your personal mobile.

14
00:00:48,715 --> 00:00:52,774
You can mute, open the keypad, or
transfer the call to a colleague.

15
00:00:53,626 --> 00:00:58,234
When you hang up, the call and its
recording are added to the conversation,

16
00:00:58,234 --> 00:01:00,998
so anyone on your team
can see what happened.

17
00:01:00,998 --> 00:01:04,930
Answered calls, missed calls and
voicemails all appear this way,

18
00:01:04,930 --> 00:01:08,064
so the inbox doubles as
your complete call history.

19
00:01:08,915 --> 00:01:11,828
If nobody answers, callers
can leave a voicemail.

20
00:01:11,828 --> 00:01:14,623
It arrives in the inbox
like any other message,

21
00:01:14,623 --> 00:01:16,941
with a player and a written transcript,

22
00:01:16,941 --> 00:01:20,390
so you can see what it's about
without even pressing play.

23
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:24,689
Noah wants to move his check-up,
so the next step is clear.

24
00:01:24,689 --> 00:01:28,899
Priya owns this conversation, and she
can call him back from right here,

25
00:01:28,899 --> 00:01:29,776
with one click.

26
00:01:30,625 --> 00:01:31,633
Now the big one.

27
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:36,609
When a call goes unanswered, most people
simply ring the next business on their

28
00:01:36,609 --> 00:01:36,924
list.

29
00:01:36,924 --> 00:01:39,002
Missed-call text-back fixes that.

30
00:01:39,002 --> 00:01:43,600
Seconds after a missed call, Kyntlo
sends a friendly text, automatically.

31
00:01:44,451 --> 00:01:45,333
And it worked.

32
00:01:45,333 --> 00:01:48,419
Instead of a lost caller,
we have a conversation,

33
00:01:48,419 --> 00:01:52,135
and a patient with a chipped
tooth asking to be seen today.

34
00:01:52,135 --> 00:01:56,291
Reply, book them in, and that
missed call has turned into revenue.

35
00:01:57,142 --> 00:01:58,986
Look at the panel on the right.

36
00:01:58,986 --> 00:02:01,306
This caller wasn't in our contacts yet,

37
00:02:01,306 --> 00:02:04,518
so Kyntlo created a new
contact from the phone number.

38
00:02:04,518 --> 00:02:06,838
Click Add name once you know who it is,

39
00:02:06,838 --> 00:02:09,931
and every future call and
message is linked to them.

40
00:02:10,782 --> 00:02:13,495
Behind the scenes, this
runs as a workflow.

41
00:02:13,495 --> 00:02:17,597
When a call is missed, the workflow
sends your text-back message.

42
00:02:17,597 --> 00:02:20,248
Bloom's is called "Missed Call Text-Back",

43
00:02:20,248 --> 00:02:23,150
and you'll build one
step by step in Module 9.

44
00:02:24,004 --> 00:02:25,102
Here's a pro tip.

45
00:02:25,102 --> 00:02:28,719
Write your text-back message
like a person, not a robot.

46
00:02:28,719 --> 00:02:33,692
Say who you are, apologise for missing
the call, and ask one simple question,

47
00:02:33,692 --> 00:02:35,177
like "How can we help?"

48
00:02:35,177 --> 00:02:38,794
A question gets far more
replies than a link on its own.

49
00:02:39,644 --> 00:02:41,349
That wraps up Conversations!

50
00:02:41,349 --> 00:02:43,784
In Module 5, we'll move on to calendars,

51
00:02:43,784 --> 00:02:48,898
starting with the different calendar types,
and which one fits each kind of booking.

52
00:02:48,898 --> 00:02:49,750
See you there.
